From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 22:58:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] kumquat: back host visible memory with shared memory on Apple

vkMapMemory asks the host to export the memory as a blob, and with external
blobs alone that is an export of the VkDeviceMemory. Metal exports memory only
as an in-process MTLBuffer or MTLTexture, which cannot be handed to another
process, so the host stops at "ExternalBlob feature is not supported with
external memory metal" and the guest waits forever for a reply.

With system blobs the host backs host visible memory with shared memory and
imports it as a host pointer, which MoltenVK supports, and the guest is handed
the shared memory descriptor it already knows how to map.
---
 kumquat/server/src/kumquat_gpu/mod.rs | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kumquat/server/src/kumquat_gpu/mod.rs b/kumquat/server/src/kumquat_gpu/mod.rs
index 4483999..a2854d4 100644
--- a/kumquat/server/src/kumquat_gpu/mod.rs
+++ b/kumquat/server/src/kumquat_gpu/mod.rs
@@ -127,6 +127,8 @@ impl KumquatGpu {
 
         let rutabaga = RutabagaBuilder::new(capset_mask, fence_handler)
             .set_use_external_blob(true)
+            // Metal cannot export memory to another process.
+            .set_use_system_blob(cfg!(target_vendor = "apple"))
             .set_use_egl(true)
             .set_wsi(RutabagaWsi::Surfaceless)
             .set_renderer_features(renderer_features_opt)
